# Input for the reproducibility lockfile. DO NOT install from this file directly —
# install from the generated `requirements.lock.txt`, which pins the full transitive
# dependency tree with hashes.
#
# These are the same direct pins as `requirements.txt` (the 2026-07-20 freeze), MINUS
# `jupyter`: notebooks are an interactive analysis tool and are not needed to regenerate
# any figure, table, or test result. Excluding it keeps the container image small and
# removes ~60 packages of resolution surface. If you ever need notebooks inside the
# container, add jupyter here and re-lock.
#
# To regenerate the lockfile, run `make lock` (do not run uv by hand — the flags matter).
#
# Note the --exclude-newer cutoff in the Makefile. Without it, resolution consults the
# live package index, so re-locking would silently pull in whatever was published since
# — and CI's "is the lockfile stale?" check would fail every time any of the 30-odd
# transitive dependencies cut a release, for no real reason. The cutoff makes the
# resolution a pure function of this file. Bump it deliberately when upgrading, then
# rebuild, re-run the suite, and record any numeric drift.
# Build backend, pinned so the editable install of budget-guard itself needs no
# network access and no unpinned build-isolation download at image build time.
setuptools==83.0.0
wheel==0.47.0

pandas==3.0.3
numpy==2.5.1
scikit-learn==1.9.0
lightgbm==4.6.0
scipy==1.18.0
matplotlib==3.11.0
pytest==9.1.1
huggingface_hub==1.22.0
